IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `s121-nouns`
IMPORT `s121-support`
IMPORT `s121-a-exclusion`
IMPORT `s121-b-limitations`

-- Tests for subsection (b). Expected values are worked out by hand from the text and the calendar, then run.

§ `Tests: (b)(1) and (b)(2)`

#ASSERT `s 121(b)(1) the dollar limitation` EQUALS 250000
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(1) the amount of gain excluded, which shall not exceed the limitation` 100000 250000 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(1) the amount of gain excluded, which shall not exceed the limitation` 250000 250000 EQUALS 250000
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(1) the amount of gain excluded, which shall not exceed the limitation` 250001 250000 EQUALS 250000
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(1) the amount of gain excluded, which shall not exceed the limitation` 500000 500000 EQUALS 500000
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(1) the amount of gain excluded, which shall not exceed the limitation` 500001 500000 EQUALS 500000

-- (b)(2)(A)(i): either spouse owns
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A)(i) either spouse meets the ownership requirements of subsection (a)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A)(i) either spouse meets the ownership requirements of subsection (a)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A)(i) either spouse meets the ownership requirements of subsection (a)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A)(i) either spouse meets the ownership requirements of subsection (a)` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A)(i) either spouse meets the ownership requirements of subsection (a)` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b)(2)(A)(ii): both spouses use
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A)(ii) both spouses meet the use requirements of subsection (a)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A)(ii) both spouses meet the use requirements of subsection (a)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A)(ii) both spouses meet the use requirements of subsection (a)` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b)(2)(A)(iii): neither is barred by paragraph (3)
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A)(iii) neither spouse is ineligible by reason of paragraph (3)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A)(iii) neither spouse is ineligible by reason of paragraph (3)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A)(iii) neither spouse is ineligible by reason of paragraph (3)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A)(iii) neither spouse is ineligible by reason of paragraph (3)` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b)(2)(A) together
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A) the limitation under paragraph (1) as substituted` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST 500000
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A) the limitation under paragraph (1) as substituted` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(A) the limitation under paragraph (1) as substituted` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b)(2)(B): what a spouse would be entitled to if not married: ownership (either spouse's period), use (own) and no bar
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation under paragraph (1) to which the spouse would be entitled if the spouses had not been married` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST 250000
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation under paragraph (1) to which the spouse would be entitled if the spouses had not been married` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation under paragraph (1) to which the spouse would be entitled if the spouses had not been married` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation under paragraph (1) to which the spouse would be entitled if the spouses had not been married` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation under paragraph (1) to which the spouse would be entitled if the spouses had not been married` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b)(2)(B): the sum of the two spouses' limitations, when (A) is not met
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation for other joint returns` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST 250000) (JUST 250000) EQUALS JUST 500000
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation for other joint returns` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST 250000) (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 250000
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation for other joint returns` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST 0) (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation for other joint returns` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST 250000) (JUST 250000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation for other joint returns` TRUE NOTHING (JUST 250000) (JUST 250000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation for other joint returns` FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST 250000) (JUST 250000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation for other joint returns` TRUE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST 250000) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests: (b)(3)`

-- Sale on 15 March 2026; the 2-year period ending on it runs from 16 March 2024 to 15 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(3) subsection (a) shall not apply because of another sale or exchange within 2 years` (Date 15 3 2026) (LIST Date 16 3 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(3) subsection (a) shall not apply because of another sale or exchange within 2 years` (Date 15 3 2026) (LIST Date 15 3 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(3) subsection (a) shall not apply because of another sale or exchange within 2 years` (Date 15 3 2026) (LIST Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(3) subsection (a) shall not apply because of another sale or exchange within 2 years` (Date 15 3 2026) (LIST Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(3) subsection (a) shall not apply because of another sale or exchange within 2 years` (Date 15 3 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(3) subsection (a) shall not apply because of another sale or exchange within 2 years` (Date 15 3 2026) (LIST Date 1 1 2015, Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Tests: (b)(4)`

-- Death on 1 March 2024; 2 years after is 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(4) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(4) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(4) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(4) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 3 2024) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(4) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a death on 29 February 2024: 29 February 2026 does not exist and rolls to 1 March 2026 (fork F5), so a sale on 1 March 2026 is in time and one on 2 March is not
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(4) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 29 2 2024) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(4) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 29 2 2024) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (2)(A) "immediately before" the death on 1 March 2024: the 5-year period ends on 29 February 2024 (2 March 2019 to 29 February 2024); 2 years ending then is 730 days.
`a test survivor held from 2015` MEANS Holding OF (LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2015), (Date 1 3 2026)), (LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2015), (Date 1 3 2026))
`a test late spouse held from 2020` MEANS Holding OF (LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 1 3 2024)), (LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 1 3 2024))
`a test late spouse used from 1 March 2023` MEANS Holding OF (LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 1 3 2024)), (LIST Span OF (Date 1 3 2023), (Date 1 3 2024))
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(4) the requirements of paragraph (2)(A) were met immediately before the date of death` `a test survivor held from 2015` `a test late spouse held from 2020` (Date 1 3 2024) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the late spouse used it only 365 days of the window: the use requirement is not met for both
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(4) the requirements of paragraph (2)(A) were met immediately before the date of death` `a test survivor held from 2015` `a test late spouse used from 1 March 2023` (Date 1 3 2024) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the late spouse sold another home on 1 June 2023, within the 2 years before: paragraph (3) bars that spouse, so (iii) fails
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(4) the requirements of paragraph (2)(A) were met immediately before the date of death` `a test survivor held from 2015` `a test late spouse held from 2020` (Date 1 3 2024) EMPTY (LIST Date 1 6 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the survivor's own earlier sale on 1 March 2022 is more than 2 years before 29 February 2024 (the period starts 2 March 2022): no bar
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(4) the requirements of paragraph (2)(A) were met immediately before the date of death` `a test survivor held from 2015` `a test late spouse held from 2020` (Date 1 3 2024) (LIST Date 1 3 2022) EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Tests: (b)(5)`

-- (D): the gain after (d)(6), for both subparagraphs
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(D)(i) the gain to which subparagraph (A) is applied after the application of subsection (d)(6)` 100000 30000 EQUALS 70000
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(D)(ii) the gain to which subparagraph (B) is applied, without regard to the gain to which (d)(6) applies` 100000 30000 EQUALS 70000
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(D)(i) the gain to which subparagraph (A) is applied after the application of subsection (d)(6)` 100000 0 EQUALS 100000

-- (C)(i): only nonqualified use from January 1, 2009. Owned 1 January 2006 to 31 December 2015, used 1 January 2006 to 31 December 2007: from 1 January 2009 to 31 December 2015 is 2556 days (2009 to 2015, with 29 February 2012).
`a test owned 2006 to 2015` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2006), (Date 31 12 2015)
`a test used 2006 to 2007` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2006), (Date 31 12 2007)
#ASSERT `the days in the spans of a list` (`s 121(b)(5)(C)(i) the periods of nonqualified use` `a test owned 2006 to 2015` `a test used 2006 to 2007`) EQUALS 2556
-- one day each side of January 1, 2009: not used 31 December 2008 and 1 January 2009 counts one day; not used 31 December 2008 alone counts none
#ASSERT `the days in the spans of a list` (`s 121(b)(5)(C)(i) the periods of nonqualified use` (LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2006), (Date 1 1 2009)) (LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2006), (Date 30 12 2008))) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the days in the spans of a list` (`s 121(b)(5)(C)(i) the periods of nonqualified use` (LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2006), (Date 31 12 2008)) (LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2006), (Date 30 12 2008))) EQUALS 0
-- all of the owned period used: no nonqualified use
#ASSERT `the days in the spans of a list` (`s 121(b)(5)(C)(i) the periods of nonqualified use` `a test owned 2006 to 2015` `a test owned 2006 to 2015`) EQUALS 0

-- (C)(ii)(I): the part of the 5-year period (16 March 2021 to 15 March 2026) after the last use. Last use 31 December 2019: the whole window is after it.
`a test window to March 2026` MEANS Span OF (Date 16 3 2021), (Date 15 3 2026)
`a test used 2012 to 2019` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2012), (Date 31 12 2019)
#ASSERT `the days in the spans of a list` (`s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(I) the portion of the 5-year period after the last date the property is used as the principal residence` `a test used 2012 to 2019` `a test window to March 2026`) EQUALS 1826
-- last use 15 March 2024: the part of the window after it is 16 March 2024 to 15 March 2026 = 730 days
#ASSERT `the days in the spans of a list` (`s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(I) the portion of the 5-year period after the last date the property is used as the principal residence` (LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2012), (Date 15 3 2024)) `a test window to March 2026`) EQUALS 730
-- last use on the sale date: nothing after it
#ASSERT `the days in the spans of a list` (`s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(I) the portion of the 5-year period after the last date the property is used as the principal residence` (LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2012), (Date 15 3 2026)) `a test window to March 2026`) EQUALS 0
-- no use at all: there is no last date (not covered), so nothing is excepted
#ASSERT `the days in the spans of a list` (`s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(I) the portion of the 5-year period after the last date the property is used as the principal residence` EMPTY `a test window to March 2026`) EQUALS 0

-- (C)(ii)(II): duty days inside the nonqualified use, capped at the days of 10 years ending on the sale (31 December 2025: 1 January 2016 to 31 December 2025 = 3653 days, leap years 2016, 2020, 2024)
`a test nonqualified 2016 to 2025` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2016), (Date 31 12 2025)
`a test nonqualified 2009 to 2025` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2009), (Date 31 12 2025)
`a test duty 2009 to 2025` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2009), (Date 31 12 2025)
`a test duty 2016 to 2025` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2016), (Date 31 12 2025)
`a test duty 2016 to 2024 and a day` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2016), (Date 30 12 2025)
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(II) the days of qualified official extended duty, not to exceed an aggregate of 10 years` `a test nonqualified 2016 to 2025` `a test duty 2016 to 2025` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS 3653
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(II) the days of qualified official extended duty, not to exceed an aggregate of 10 years` `a test nonqualified 2016 to 2025` `a test duty 2016 to 2024 and a day` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS 3652
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(II) the days of qualified official extended duty, not to exceed an aggregate of 10 years` `a test nonqualified 2009 to 2025` `a test duty 2009 to 2025` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS 3653
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(II) the days of qualified official extended duty, not to exceed an aggregate of 10 years` `a test nonqualified 2009 to 2025` EMPTY (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS 0

-- (C)(ii)(III): temporary absence for employment, health or unforeseen circumstances, capped at 2 years ending on the sale date (31 December 2021: 1 January 2020 to 31 December 2021 = 731 days)
`a test nonqualified 2012 to 2021` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2012), (Date 31 12 2021)
`a test absence of 2020 for health` MEANS LIST (`Temporary absence` WITH
    `days` IS (Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 31 12 2020))
    `change of employment` IS FALSE
    `health conditions` IS TRUE
    `unforeseen circumstances as may be specified by the Secretary` IS FALSE)
`a test absence of 2012 to 2021 for employment` MEANS LIST (`Temporary absence` WITH
    `days` IS (Span OF (Date 1 1 2012), (Date 31 12 2021))
    `change of employment` IS TRUE
    `health conditions` IS FALSE
    `unforeseen circumstances as may be specified by the Secretary` IS FALSE)
`a test absence of 2020 for no listed reason` MEANS LIST (`Temporary absence` WITH
    `days` IS (Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 31 12 2020))
    `change of employment` IS FALSE
    `health conditions` IS FALSE
    `unforeseen circumstances as may be specified by the Secretary` IS FALSE)
`a test absence of 2020 for an unforeseen circumstance` MEANS LIST (`Temporary absence` WITH
    `days` IS (Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 31 12 2020))
    `change of employment` IS FALSE
    `health conditions` IS FALSE
    `unforeseen circumstances as may be specified by the Secretary` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(III) the days of other temporary absence, not to exceed an aggregate of 2 years` `a test nonqualified 2012 to 2021` `a test absence of 2020 for health` (Date 31 12 2021) EQUALS 366
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(III) the days of other temporary absence, not to exceed an aggregate of 2 years` `a test nonqualified 2012 to 2021` `a test absence of 2012 to 2021 for employment` (Date 31 12 2021) EQUALS 731
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(III) the days of other temporary absence, not to exceed an aggregate of 2 years` `a test nonqualified 2012 to 2021` `a test absence of 2020 for no listed reason` (Date 31 12 2021) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(III) the days of other temporary absence, not to exceed an aggregate of 2 years` `a test nonqualified 2012 to 2021` `a test absence of 2020 for an unforeseen circumstance` (Date 31 12 2021) EQUALS 366

-- (C) altogether, scenario 1: owned 1 January 2012 to 15 March 2026, used 1 January 2012 to 31 December 2019, sale 15 March 2026.
-- Nonqualified: 1 January 2020 to 15 March 2026; excepted: the window 16 March 2021 on; left 1 January 2020 to 15 March 2021 = 366 + 74 = 440 days.
`a test owned 2012 to 2026` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2012), (Date 15 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(C) the aggregate days of nonqualified use` `a test owned 2012 to 2026` `a test used 2012 to 2019` `a test used 2012 to 2019` `a test window to March 2026` (Date 15 3 2026) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS 440
-- scenario 2: used 2012 to 2014 and again 2020 to the sale; away on qualified official extended duty 2015 to 2019 (1826 days): all of the gap is excepted
`a test used 2012 to 2014 and 2020 to 2026` MEANS LIST
    Span OF (Date 1 1 2012), (Date 31 12 2014)
    Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 15 3 2026)
`a test duty 2015 to 2019` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2015), (Date 31 12 2019)
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(C) the aggregate days of nonqualified use` `a test owned 2012 to 2026` `a test used 2012 to 2014 and 2020 to 2026` `a test used 2012 to 2014 and 2020 to 2026` `a test window to March 2026` (Date 15 3 2026) `a test duty 2015 to 2019` EMPTY EQUALS 0
-- scenario 3: used 2012 to 2014 and 2019 on; duty 2015 and 2016 (731 days), absent for health in 2017 (365), vacant in 2018 (365): only the vacant year is nonqualified use
`a test used 2012 to 2014 and 2019 to 2026` MEANS LIST
    Span OF (Date 1 1 2012), (Date 31 12 2014)
    Span OF (Date 1 1 2019), (Date 15 3 2026)
`a test duty 2015 to 2016` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2015), (Date 31 12 2016)
`a test absence of 2017 for health` MEANS LIST (`Temporary absence` WITH
    `days` IS (Span OF (Date 1 1 2017), (Date 31 12 2017))
    `change of employment` IS FALSE
    `health conditions` IS TRUE
    `unforeseen circumstances as may be specified by the Secretary` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(C) the aggregate days of nonqualified use` `a test owned 2012 to 2026` `a test used 2012 to 2014 and 2019 to 2026` `a test used 2012 to 2014 and 2019 to 2026` `a test window to March 2026` (Date 15 3 2026) `a test duty 2015 to 2016` `a test absence of 2017 for health` EQUALS 365

-- (B): the ratio. 440 days of nonqualified use in 5188 days owned (14 years from 1 January 2012 with 4 leap days, 5114, plus 74).
#ASSERT `the days in the spans of a list` `a test owned 2012 to 2026` EQUALS 5188
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(B) the ratio of the aggregate periods of nonqualified use to the period owned` 440 5188 EQUALS JUST (440 DIVIDED BY 5188)
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(B) the ratio of the aggregate periods of nonqualified use to the period owned` 0 5188 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(B) the ratio of the aggregate periods of nonqualified use to the period owned` 5188 5188 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(B) the ratio of the aggregate periods of nonqualified use to the period owned` 10 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (A): the gain allocated is the gain times the ratio
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(A) the gain to which subsection (a) shall not apply, being the gain allocated to periods of nonqualified use` 100000 (JUST (1 DIVIDED BY 4)) EQUALS JUST 25000
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(A) the gain to which subsection (a) shall not apply, being the gain allocated to periods of nonqualified use` 100000 (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 121(b)(5)(A) the gain to which subsection (a) shall not apply, being the gain allocated to periods of nonqualified use` 100000 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
